+# Official ReSkate update with native Throwdowns retained
+
+## Update to 2.0.6 on 11 October 2026
+
+Official tag `v2.0.6`, commit `314d31fe7bf73866b4ae9b6a8195de50ced26312`,
+is merged into the custom branch. Four conflicts were resolved by retaining
+the custom camera activation include and corrected protocol fixture offsets,
+adding the upstream first-person cycle include and teleport command check.
+The native custom pack remains embedded and uses official multiplayer protocol
+49. Both launcher and DLL report 2.0.6. Binary auto-updates remain disabled.
+
+The custom waiting HUD now saves native callbacks before publishing its private
+presenter. Map and respawn pose interruptions keep the loaded-world lobby alive.
+The distant registration icon imports bind to the matching approved challenge
+logo, with all 45 dependencies resident in owning level bundles. An incorrect
+entity-query hook was removed after offline decompilation disproved its role.
+
+All 77 regression tests pass, including the new map interruption/Start/Leave
+coordinator cases. Build and validation logs: `../reskate-206-build.log`,
+`../reskate-206-final-runtime-build.log`, `../reskate-206-ctest.log`.
+The DLL's embedded archive was verified as data without execution. Archive SHA256:
+`bd359876f83796f13b091e7a06cc329d3464e5cf98d8f62d895ee8a92f25cbc7`.
+See `contrib/throwdown-flags/README.md` for asset contracts and pending manual
+confirmation. Throwdown Panel and native celebration work remain deferred.
+
+## Source provenance
+
+Official release: [v2.0.3](https://github.com/Dingo-Shenanigans/ReSkate/releases/tag/v2.0.3), commit `5b7395c3ac189e992de5d7767be2b8dfb0b7695a`, published 2026-10-10 18:41:13 UTC.
+
+The existing runtime source is closest to official commit `62082426cb7d5414d557f28d2a35089cbe7a7da7` from October 6 (1,067 matching original files, 62 modified files). The supplied mode fork `f3316c1` includes official v2.0.2 history, but its game modes had been adapted into this older runtime. Treating the entire runtime as v2.0.2 would have preserved accidental reversions of newer upstream features.
+
+All 1,222 existing source/asset files were copied and SHA-256 verified before merging, including the embedded native asset pack. The backup is `../reskate-pre-v2.0.3-source/`; its file manifest is `../reskate-pre-v2.0.3-manifest.json`. The separate integration repository is `../reskate-upstream-merge/`, branch `native-throwdowns-preserved`. It contains a commit with the exact customized source on the original upstream baseline, then the v2.0.3 merge. This is a local source backup, not a published branch or ZIP.
+
+The merge was normalized for line endings, then 41 conflicting blocks in 26 files were reviewed. Decisions are recorded in `../reskate-v2.0.3-conflict-resolutions.json`. The source installation manifest is `../reskate-v2.0.3-source-install.json`. Launcher code and ordinary upstream features are updated; the custom Throwdown source, private Rime assets, landed-trick scoring, native flag bridge, solo queue cleanup, marker restrictions, custom relay handlers and native picker remain included.
+
+## Compatibility and update behavior
+
+- Build version: `2.0.3-throwdowns-dev`, stamped into both the DLL and launcher.
+- `DINGOSDK_LAUNCHER_AUTO_UPDATE=OFF`: the launcher retains upstream functionality but will not replace this custom DLL with the stock release. Future updates need the same source merge/rebuild process.
+- Upstream multiplayer protocol: **47**. Official older clients/servers are incompatible with v2.0.3.
+- Custom mode message version: **10**, carrying explicit finish-line state and each racer's remaining time. Custom mode participants need this same pack build.
+- The existing 1-Up wire format remains distinct from the imported generic mode rules.
+- Current native pack archive: SHA-256 `a0df97490c35bdefb9842b986be9a177e333ba0f83fc76db4cfb1ea61b97f86d`, 15 files, 107,811,233 bytes. The source archive embeds the approved badges, corrected private selection graph and native Deathrace objects; the latest Release build and verification are described below.
