+Deathrace feedback follow-up: remove the redundant Start flag selector; rotate with D-pad left/right; resize the complete gate with up/down; save with Start; undo with Y. Three native start dumps faulted while a non-model asset was passed to the native DataModelObject loader, so the supported loader now rejects non-record assets before its unchecked TypeInfo reads and logs the offending asset. This is a diagnostic crash guard; it does not prove the panel or race starts correctly live. Release build and all 73 regression tests passed. The official Spot Battle ending was captured at selection 9 with two celebration models; the custom native ending bridge remains unfinished.
+
+Deathrace gameplay follow-up: live feedback confirms starting no longer crashes, but gates were waiting for the already accepted native flag at route point zero. Racers now begin at point one. Segment-plane interpolation accepts fast crossings between samples and retains the exact gate width/height check; the referee still rejects duplicates, skipped gates and expired clocks. The editor groups LT/RT, rotation and sizing pairs, uses X for Undo to match the native glyph, and separates controls from the Deathrace logo/title. Gameplay shows an individual clock and a compact middle-left native list with place suffixes, player names, time and the existing crown/rough row styling; it does not use the broken legacy score/profile bindings. Deathrace finish results reuse those valid time rows.
+
+The private native panel resolves records explicitly in Context's locked manager instead of the expression wrapper's TLS manager. Authored/runtime TypeInfo aliases require identical hashes, sizes, field order, offsets and recursively matched child schemas. Its player list uses native Label presenters matching their actual data. The upstream S.K.A.T.E. adapter retains the game's native activity rule and backend/menu flow; custom matches retire their setup registration and therefore still need a manual check of the native pause transition, shortcut and Quit. Full native ending celebration and multiplayer admission remain unfinished.
